  "title": "P-ary m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from Martínez-Cagigal et al. (2023)",
  "description": "A derivative EEG dataset comprising code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) recordings from 16 healthy subjects using p-ary m-sequences for brain-computer interface applications. The dataset contains 5 sessions per subject with 8 runs each, recorded at 256 Hz from 16 EEG channels across 11 stimulus classes. This dataset supports research on non-binary m-sequence-based paradigms designed to enhance user comfort in c-VEP-based BCIs.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired at a sampling rate of 256 Hz using 16 channels with standard 1005 montage. The experimental paradigm employed code-modulated visual evoked potentials with p-ary m-sequences across 11 classes (0-10). Each session contained 8 runs (6 training, 2 testing) with a trial interval of 0-1 second. Line frequency was 50 Hz.",
